# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data must never enter this repository.
#
# The EHR extract is governed by an IRB data-use agreement. The rules below
# deny by directory and by extension, so an accidental `git add` of a data file
# or a derived cache fails rather than publishing it.
#
# Do not add exceptions without checking what the file actually contains:
# per-record predictions, label vectors and metric tables built from them are
# individual-level data too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- directories the code reads from and writes to --------------------------
# These are the defaults in */paths.py (CKD_RAW_ROOT, CKD_DATA_ROOT,
# CKD_RESULT_ROOT, CKD_WORK_DIR). Point the variables elsewhere and those
# locations are outside the repository anyway.
data/
data_local/
result/
work/
outputs/
checkpoints/
logs/

# --- serialised data and model weights, wherever they land ------------------
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.npz
*.npy
*.parquet
*.feather
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.sav

# --- tabular exports --------------------------------------------------------
# Every CSV/Excel file this pipeline touches is either the hospital export or a
# per-slice prediction table. Nothing in version control needs to be one.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Run directories store predictions as result.json / *_result.pkl
result.json
*_result.json

# --- TensorBoard (event files embed the training host name) -----------------
events.out.tfevents.*
runs/

# --- figures ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Curves are drawn from per-patient predictions; regenerate them rather than
# committing them.
*.png
*.pdf
*.svg

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- one-off local tooling --------------------------------------------------
# Migration helper for datasets built before the reduced24_* naming was
# unified. Run it once against your data directory; it is not part of the
# published pipeline.
rename_reduced224.sh

# --- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
